aurora_fifo_profile: where the GX FIFO worker's time goes

The 60 fps mode (docs/FPS60_PLAN.md) has the FIFO worker translate two paints per game frame; on the
Switch at 1020 MHz it is the limit (Dragon Roost). A sampling profile: the translating thread stores its
current category (parse, frame jobs, BP/XF/CP loads, Aurora subcommands, draws and their pipeline
lookup, bind groups, uniforms, indexed arrays, draw command; one relaxed byte store per scope) and a
sampler thread adds the time since its last sample to the category it finds, every ~250 us. Per-scope
clock reads were tried first and tripled the worker's time on the Mac. Plus counts and byte totals.
Off by default (no stores, no sampler thread): aurora_fifo_profile_enable(true); the game reads the
running totals with aurora_fifo_profile_get (native: COS_FIFO_PROFILE=1, a perf line).diff --git a/include/aurora/aurora.h b/include/aurora/aurora.h
